WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:08.220
An ordinary three D model shows you an object. A demonstration shows you how it works. Interaction Twin connects the two.

2
00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:22.664
Record an everyday interaction, and turn it into a source-linked object program: the parts, their connections, and what happened. Your agent can inspect that knowledge, follow its evidence, and reuse it.

3
00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:37.455
Combine a phone and charger from separate recordings. Describe a new task, then rehearse it in three D before physical validation. Show an interaction once. Keep how it works.

4
00:00:45.400 --> 00:01:00.641
The library turns recorded demonstrations into objects you can explore. Compare source video with connected replay, inspect individual parts, and download geometry and descriptive files. Every example keeps its evidence close.

5
00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:18.074
An object program adds meaning to geometry. It describes which parts belong together, which relationships are estimated, and which actions were observed. Source references are preserved, while unknown physical properties stay explicit.

6
00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:32.332
Muse proposes the structure. Separate prompts ask the same model to critique it alongside code checks. Repairs can follow, before the owner approves the exact revision.

7
00:01:35.300 --> 00:01:46.474
That knowledge reaches an agent through a local, read-only M C P server. The agent can search, inspect interfaces, retrieve geometry, and follow source evidence.

8
00:01:48.300 --> 00:02:01.428
The phone and charger make reuse concrete. A saved client inspected two recordings and prepared a shared task draft. Those interface matches are candidates; compatibility still needs independent validation.

9
00:02:03.350 --> 00:02:25.464
The preview makes a proposed task easier to inspect. The case and earbuds become a complete, editable rehearsal. The source recording remains available for comparison. Then the same approach brings the phone and charger into one scene. These authored kinematics communicate an idea before contact, insertion, and hardware execution are validated.

10
00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:48.530
Meta's models provide perception and proposals: Muse for structure, SAM for segmentation, and SAM three D for component drafts. Our code builds source-linked object programs, manages checks, review and approval, and exposes the results through viewers and M C P.

11
00:02:49.300 --> 00:02:58.666
The next step is physical validation. The foundation is inspectable: real demonstrations, reusable object knowledge. Interaction Twin.
